{title: 554 - O Let Me Walk With Thee}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[D7]Olet [G]me walk with [Am/C]Thee, my [D7]God,
[G]As [Em]Enoch [C]walked in days of old;
[G]Place Thou my [C/G]trembling hand in Thine,
[G]And [C]sweet communion [D]with me hold;
[G]E’en though the [C/G]path I may not see,
[C]Yet, [G]Jesus, let [D]me [D7]walk [G/D]with [D]Thee.

Verse 2:
[D7]I [G]cannot, dare not, [Am/C]walk alone;
[G]The [Em]tempest [C]rages in the sky,
[G]A thousand [C/G]snares beset my [G]feet,
[G]A [C]thousand [G]foes are [D]lurking nigh.
[G]Still Thou the [C/G]raging of the sea,
[C]O [G]Master! let [D]me [D7]walk [G/D]with [D]Thee.

Verse 3:
[D7]If [G]I may rest my [Am/C]hand in [D7]Thine,
[G]I'll [Em]count the [C]joys of earth but loss,
[G]And firmly, [C/G]bravely journey [G]on;
[G]I'll [C]bear the [G]banner [D]of the cross
[G]Till Zion's glorious [C/G]gates I see;
[C]Yet, [G]Savior, let [D]me [D7]walk [G/D]with [D]Thee.
